From: OpenATV RetroGaming Maintainers <noreply@openatv.org>
Subject: [PATCH] libmpeg2: preserve toolchain file offset selection

OpenEmbedded builds 32-bit targets with 64-bit time and file offsets.  The
bundled generated config header unconditionally undefines
_FILE_OFFSET_BITS after the compiler has set it, which glibc correctly
rejects when _TIME_BITS remains 64.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [OpenEmbedded toolchain integration]

---
 deps/libmpeg2/include/config.h | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/deps/libmpeg2/include/config.h b/deps/libmpeg2/include/config.h
index eb15f8d..f6c4d22 100644
--- a/deps/libmpeg2/include/config.h
+++ b/deps/libmpeg2/include/config.h
@@ -145,8 +145,6 @@
 /* Define to 1 if the X Window System is missing or not being used. */
 #undef X_DISPLAY_MISSING
 
-/* Number of bits in a file offset, on hosts where this is settable. */
-#undef _FILE_OFFSET_BITS
 
 /* Define for large files, on AIX-style hosts. */
 #undef _LARGE_FILES
-- 
2.43.0
